    "developer-opening": "{\"questions\":[{\"question\":\"Does the text open with something that happened to a developer, such as a specific event or experience involving a developer (for example, \\\"Last Tuesday, a developer on our team deleted the production database\\\")? A general statement about developers, a claim about the industry, or a question to the reader (for example, \\\"Developers face constant pressure to ship faster\\\") doesn't count.\",\"passes\":\"yes\"}]}",
    "no-hype": "{\"questions\":[{\"question\":\"Does the text use hype words to promote or praise something, such as \\\"revolutionary\\\", \\\"game-changing\\\", or similar over-the-top buzzwords? Words that are only quoted or mentioned in order to discuss or criticize them (e.g. 'the label \\\"revolutionary\\\" is overused') don't count as the text using them.\",\"passes\":\"no\"}]}",
    "a-number": "{\"questions\":[{\"question\":\"Does the text support its main point with a specific number, such as a statistic, measurement, count, or percentage? A figure that backs the claim counts (e.g. \\\"load time dropped 40%\\\" or \\\"3 of 5 users quit\\\"). Vague quantity words (\\\"many\\\", \\\"most\\\", \\\"a lot\\\") and numbers unrelated to the point (like a date or a list's numbering) don't count.\",\"passes\":\"yes\"}]}"
  },
